    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d626">

                <pb facs="0881" n="869" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg869"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Japan)/11–2645</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of the Australian Legation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Oldham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 515/45</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-26">26 November,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour, in the absence of the
                    Minister, to refer to my letter to you of 24th November, 1945<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d626-f1"/> relative to the participation of British Commonwealth
                    forces in the occupation of Japan and to inform you that the Minister of State
                    for External Affairs, Dr. H. V. Evatt, and, as his alternate, the Minister of
                    Australia, Sir Frederic Eggleston, together with Lt. General Sir John Lavarack
                    will act as the Australian representatives in the discussions regarding the
                    participation of the Commonwealth forces.</p>
                <p>I have been instructed to add that it is the earnest desire of the Australian
                    Government that the above discussions will be initiated with the utmost
                    despatch.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Oldham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d626-f1" n="41" xml:id="d626-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it acknowledged receipt of Department’s note dated November 23, <ref
                        target="#pg863">p. 863</ref>.</p>
            </note>
